 | style="text-align: center" | [[File:Collectible Spoon Bender tears.png|50px|link=#Homing]]
 | Completely diverts from their original path to seek nearby enemies. The distance homing tears can travel is determined by the [[range]] stat.{{dlc|nr}} The friction of {{i|Sacred Heart}}'s and {{i|Seraphim}}'s homing effects have a lower value than other sources of homing, meaning the tears won't go as far.
 |-
 ! [[#Piercing|Piercing]]
 | style="text-align: center" | [[File:Collectible Cupid's Arrow tears.png|50px|link=#Piercing]]
 | style="text-align: left" |Can travel through enemies (but not obstacles) without breaking on impact.  Once a single target or a segment of an enemy has been hit by a piercing tear, it can no longer take damage from that tear.<br>{{dlc|nr}} However, piercing effects also remove [[knockback]].
 |-
 ! [[#Spectral|Spectral]]
 | style="text-align: center" | [[File:Collectible Ouija Board tears.png|50px|link=#Spectral]]
 | style="text-align: left" | Can travel through obstacles (but not enemies) without breaking on impact. Spectral tears can be used to safely dispatch most types of [[monsters]] from behind obstacles, or over them in combination with [[Flight|flying]].<br>Allows tears to pass through both enemies and obstacles if combined with Piercing.
 |-
 ! [[#Bouncing|Bouncing]]
 | style="text-align: center" | [[File:Boucing tear.png|50px|link=#Bouncing]]
 | Makes tears bounce off walls, [[Enemy|enemies]] and [[Obstacle|environmental objects]]. Tears that bounce off of enemies bounce in random directions, whereas tears that bounce off of walls and other objects bounce directly back. When tears bounce from enemies, they become able to hit the same enemy again should they bounce off of another enemy or obstacle.
 |}

